indications_limitations:
&lt;p&gt;Granulocyte transfusions to patients suffering from severe infection and granulocytopenia are a covered service under Medicare. Granulocytopenia is usually identified as fewer than 500 granulocytes&sol;mm&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;&sol;sup&gt; whole blood. Accepted indications for granulocyte transfusions include:&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;   
&lt;li&gt;Granulocytopenia with evidence of gram negative sepsis; and&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;Granulocytopenia in febrile patients with local progressive infections unresponsive to appropriate antibiotic therapy, thought to be due to gram negative organisms.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
